===Etymology===
{{wikipedia}}
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|amphora|||lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ἀμφορεύς||vased shaped ornament with a narrow neck|lang=grc|tr=amphoreus|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|amphorae|pl2=amphoras}}

# {{countable}} A two [[handle]]d [[jar]] with a [[narrow]] [[neck]] that was used in [[ancient]] times to store or carry [[wine]] or [[oil]]s.

